dialect protocol
protocol xml.snapshot
version 1
schema stdio.xml
start body

# P2-FG1: `stdio.xml` is TEXT-NATIVE (per the P2 plan's own classification, W0 census row) -- there
# is no "binary XML"; the pack container IS the SEMIO envelope wrapping the artifact's own real
# wire text verbatim (`ArtifactPack::encode_pack_with` in ../../🦀️.rs:
# `xml_document_to_text(&self.doc).into_bytes()` passed straight to `store::semio_format::
# wrap_binary` -- no `pack_rt::encode_document` structured record, because `XmlNode` is a
# genuinely recursive, data-carrying enum with no `RecordSpec` to walk against, same reason
# `#[derive(dsl::DslArtifact)]` is unusable here). Replaces the pre-Phase-2 placeholder that
# (falsely) described the payload as a JSON serialization of `XmlDocument` -- the real codec was
# fixed this wave to stop routing through `serde_json` at all (see `../../🦀️.rs`'s
# `ArtifactPack` impl doc comment), so this file's own description now matches reality.
#
# The framework-level SEMIO envelope itself (magic `0x8953454D0D0A1A0A` + LE u32 token length +
# UTF-8 token) is described ONCE, at
# `🧰️framework/🛍️products/💻️os/🔨️modules/🧬️semio/📡️protocol/📡️.protocol.semio`
# (P2-M3 deliverable 3) -- this file does NOT re-describe that framing. Cross-artifact `use
# semio.envelope` is not yet functional (confirmed unchanged through every pilot, see
# `📖️grammar-recipe.md` §2.1), so the envelope is deliberately NOT re-inlined here either -- this
# file models the bytes as if the walk already starts AT the payload, past the envelope, matching
# how `m5_handcrafted_protocol_conformance`'s own harness unwraps the envelope before handing bytes
# to `walk_protocol`.
#
# The payload itself is opaque, unstructured UTF-8 bytes at the BINARY layer by construction (its
# real internal grammar -- element/attribute/content-node recursion -- is
# ../📝️text/📖️.grammar.semio's job, not the protocol dialect's; XML nesting has no fixed
# byte width to declare here) -- `chain ... utf8` is the honest boundary, the same treatment
# json's own snapshot protocol gives its RFC8259 text payload.
framing record
chain payload utf8
